Z||000000||BAM-BAM||10-09-2000||10:25 AM||||   Are the rear quarter panels behind the doors all the same for the Coupes, SE's and GT's? I need to replace my right rear on my 85GT. LMK<P>  Sorry and Thanks, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||5
Z||000001||Tigger||10-09-2000||10:43 AM||||The panels I believe are all the same.  Only difference is the GT's have a lower rocker piece riveted in the lower part of the panel.  If you find one from a coupe or SE you'll just need to locate and drill the holes and attach the rocker piece.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">          <BR> <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||10-09-2000||10:45 AM||||Yes they are all the same, the only thing is that the models with ground effects needed two holes in the 1/4 panel.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
